{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504275392,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTQ2NTQzOTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1783","origin":"github"},"title":"Replace credential management with something simpler/more focused","message":"Re discussion at last meeting: We could switch to `pass`/pypass to have datalad manage the credentials it needs for its own purpose. We would be free to implement and naming scheme, would have the chance to search and list particular credentials.\n\n`pass` uses a directory with GPG encrypted files as a password store. `annex` already relies on GPG, so there would be no additional dependency. `pass` is merely a bash script. `pypass` is a simple reimplementation of `pass`. Before we start doing something from scratch, we should consider using/building upon `pypass`.","files":null}]}